The original does a linear scan over the whole message table on every lookup. This version builds a 65536-entry direct-index table once and then answers each lookup with a single array read.

- **Thread safety:** the table is a function-local static, so C++11 guarantees its one-time initialization is thread-safe.
- **Source data:** it is built only from the constant `mesgs` array, not from any mutable global state.
- **Duplicate numbers:** if two entries share a message number, only the first is recorded. This keeps the original "first match wins" behavior.
- **Not found:** an unused slot holds `0xFFFF`, which returns `NULL` as before.
- **Cost:** the table uses 128 KB of memory.

```cpp
const Profile::MESG* Profile::GetMesg(const FIT_UINT16 num)
{
    struct Index
    {
        FIT_UINT16 idx[65536];
        Index()
        {
            for (int k = 0; k < 65536; k++)
                idx[k] = 0xFFFF;
            for (int i = 0; i < MESGS; i++)
            {
                FIT_UINT16 n = mesgs[i].num;
                if (idx[n] == 0xFFFF)
                    idx[n] = (FIT_UINT16)i;
            }
        }
    };
    static const Index table;

    FIT_UINT16 i = table.idx[num];
    if (i == 0xFFFF)
        return NULL;
    return &mesgs[i];
}
```